# Hard Rules Verification Checklist — 6-STEP MANDATORY PIPELINE

## HARD RULE — Never mark a task "verified" without the full 6-step pipeline

A task may ONLY be marked "verified" or "done" in PLAN.md when **all six
screenshots** (3 isolated + 3 in-game) exist on disk, have been read with the
Read tool, and their paths are cited in PLAN.md. If ANY step is missing:

- The task status MUST remain "in-progress" or "code done, verify pending".
- You MUST NOT write "verified", "PASS", "done", or tick `[x]` on the task.
- If a previous session marked a task "verified" without the full pipeline,
  you MUST re-run the missing steps BEFORE relying on that status.
- A "verified" status with fewer than 6 screenshots on disk is a **rule
  violation** and the task must be reopened.

This applies retroactively: any task marked "verified" in a prior session that
does not have all 6 screenshot paths in PLAN.md must be re-verified from
scratch (isolated BEFORE/AFTER/COMPARE + in-game BEFORE/AFTER/COMPARE).

## HARD RULE — Screenshots are the PRIMARY verification, never skippable
The 6 screenshots (3 isolated + 3 in-game) are the AUTHORITATIVE proof that a
change landed. No other evidence may replace them:
- FPS numbers / perf metrics / report JSON fields alone are NOT verification.
- A code review, parse check, or "I read the diff" is NOT verification.
- "The change is obviously correct" / "the before is obvious" is NOT a reason
  to skip a capture.
You MUST have isolated AND in-game screenshots on disk, read with the Read
tool, for EVERY task. If a step genuinely cannot be captured (e.g. a one-time
first-launch behavior), say so explicitly in PLAN.md and capture the closest
possible proxy — never silently drop the step.

## HARD RULE — Multi-hero changes must be verified on EVERY affected hero
When a change touches a shared mechanic that applies to MULTIPLE heroes (the
game has **16 heroes**: Tobor, Arclight, Bulwark, Warden/Diord, Cinder, Pyra,
Slag, Ember, Thorn, Willow, Stump, Sage, Volt, Nebula, Astral, Rime), you MUST
verify it on EVERY hero that uses that code path — not just a sample.
- Run the in-game probe with `-Hero <id>` for EACH affected hero.
- "It works for Arclight" is NOT enough when the same code path runs for all 16.
- Document the per-hero results in PLAN.md (hero → observed → expected → PASS/FAIL).
- Isolated tests may cover the mechanic once; IN-GAME verification must cover
  all affected heroes.

## HARD RULE — Large tasks must be built AND verified multiple times
For LARGE tasks (multiple files, multiple heroes, multiple sub-items):
- Build incrementally; verify EACH sub-item independently.
- After the full build, re-run ALL sub-item verifications together.
- Never mark a large task done after a single screenshot batch.

Before marking ANY task as verified/complete, you MUST have a checklist entry
for each of the following. If ANY box is unchecked, the task is NOT done.

## Pre-verification checklist (run this EVERY time, for ALL tasks, no exceptions)

```
ISOLATED (do these FIRST, before ANY in-game test):
[ ] 1.  Isolated BEFORE screenshot on disk (pre-change state, isolated scene)
[ ] 2.  Isolated AFTER screenshot on disk (post-change state, isolated scene)
[ ] 3.  Isolated COMPARE — diff or side-by-side read, both images opened +
        concrete pixel differences stated in writing

IN-GAME (only after all 3 isolated steps are green):
[ ] 4.  In-game BEFORE screenshot on disk (pre-change state, real game)
[ ] 5.  In-game AFTER screenshot on disk (post-change state, real game)
[ ] 6.  In-game COMPARE — diff or side-by-side read, both images opened +
        concrete pixel differences stated in writing

FINALIZE:
[ ] 7.  ALL 6 screenshots read with the Read tool; described what is ACTUALLY shown
[ ] 8.  Report JSON verdict is PASS / expected fields match
[ ] 9.  PLAN.md status updated, referencing all 6 screenshot paths
[ ] 10. All 6+ screenshots + report JSONs committed to git and pushed
[ ] 11. App restarted with tools/restart_app.ps1 so user sees the change live
```

## How to use

1. Before starting a task, copy the checklist into your todo list.
2. Tick each box as you complete it. Do NOT start any in-game step until
   boxes 1–3 are all ticked.
3. If you cannot tick a box, the task is NOT done — note what is missing.
4. **Never** mark a task "verified" or "complete" in PLAN.md with any box unchecked.
5. **Never** skip the BEFORE screenshots. If you already made the code change,
   you MUST temporarily revert to capture the before state (both isolated AND in-game).
6. **Never** rely on the report JSON alone — you must open each PNG with the
   Read tool and describe what you see.
7. **Never** leave screenshots uncommitted. Run `git add tools/selftest/results/`
   and commit + push after every verification batch.

## Common mistakes to avoid

- Marking a task done based on "the report says PASS" without reading the screenshots.
- Skipping the isolated test and going straight to the full game.
- Capturing only an "after" screenshot without a "before" for comparison.
- Forgetting the COMPARE step: just having before+after is NOT enough; you must
  actually open both and state the visible difference.
- Forgetting to commit the result PNGs and report JSON to git.
- Not restarting the app at the end of the turn.
- Using a single screenshot to "verify" a multi-phase feature.
